-- title:
--   Rank-one freeness and multiplicity one for a commutative operator algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $W$ a finite-dimensional $K$-vector space, and let $V : \iota \to \mathrm{Submodule}\,K\,W$ be a family of subspaces indexed by a finite type $\iota$ which is supremum-independent (`iSupIndep V`) and whose supremum is all of $W$, so that $W$ is the internal direct sum of the $V_i$. Let $A$ be a $K$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_K W$ whose elements commute pairwise ($ab = ba$ for all $a, b \in A$) and which stabilises each summand: $a v \in V_i$ whenever $a \in A$, $v \in V_i$. Assume given $e : \iota \to A$ with $e_i$ acting as the identity on $V_i$ and as $0$ on $V_j$ for every $j \neq i$, and vectors $w_i \in V_i$ such that each $V_i$ is cyclic over $A$ generated by $w_i$, in the sense that every $v \in V_i$ is of the form $a(w_i)$ for some $a \in A$. Assume finally that for every $i$ and every $K$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : A \to K$ the intersection of $V_i$ with the joint eigenspace $\bigsqcap_{a \in A} \ker(a - \chi(a))$ has $K$-dimension at most $1$. The conclusion has two parts: $W$ admits a basis indexed by `Fin 1` as a module over $A$ (it is free of rank one over $A$), and for every $K$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : A \to K$ the joint eigenspace $\bigsqcap_{a \in A} \ker(a - \chi(a))$ has $K$-dimension exactly $1$.
--
--   This is the linear-algebra form of the statement that a commutative algebra of operators with separating idempotents, cyclic summands and at most one-dimensional joint eigenspaces on each summand makes the ambient space a free module of rank one, with every character occurring with multiplicity exactly one; the content beyond the hypotheses is the lower bound $\dim_K W_\chi \geq 1$. It is applied in [`CuspForm.nonempty_basis_fin_one_gammaH_and_finrank_eigenspace_eq_one`](thm.html#CuspForm.nonempty_basis_fin_one_gammaH_and_finrank_eigenspace_eq_one) to a space of cusp forms viewed as a module over a commutative Hecke algebra.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_End_nonempty_basis_fin_one_and_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_eq_one_of_iSupIndep_of_cyclic.lean

